  "title": "Outpatient psychotherapy",
  "description": "Outpatient psychotherapy is a treatment where you work with a trained mental health professional in regular office visits to address emotional, behavioral, or mental health challenges. Your therapist uses various evidence-based techniques to help you understand your thoughts and feelings, develop coping strategies, and make positive changes in your life. Psychotherapy can help with depression, anxiety, trauma, relationship issues, and many other concerns. This type of procedure can be performed various ways, including group therapy and 1:1 therapy, and the cost may vary depending on the specific approach or service provided.",
